{{/*
  The one source of the legal text (Phase 3.4, plan 08, D-31, D-27). Two partials
  render the Disclaimer and the Policy for the standalone /disclaimer and /policy
  pages, the in app reader window and, in plan 10, the scroll box of the first
  time flow, so what people agree to cannot drift from what is published.

  The dot is a LegalText value. It holds the server settings the text reads
  (numbers, contact address, expiry hours, glossary) and nothing about an account
  (R-07). Wording changes here only when the owner agrees the new text; when it
  does, policyLastUpdated and service.CurrentTermsVersion change with it.
*/}}
{{define "legal_disclaimer_body"}}
    <h2 id="disclaimer">Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>Pinalert is unofficial. It isn't a government service, and it isn't connected to any government agency or emergency service.</p>

    <h2>Pinalert is not a substitute for emergency services</h2>
    <p>Pinalert can't send help. If someone is in danger, call the emergency number first. Post here afterwards if you want to.</p>

    <h2 id="emergency-numbers">Emergency numbers</h2>
    <p>Check these numbers on your own state government's website. They can change.</p>
    <section class="legal-numbers" aria-labelledby="emergency-numbers">
      <div class="legal-numbers__row">
        <a class="legal-numbers__call" href="{{.CallHref}}" aria-label="Call {{.Numbers.Primary}}">{{.Numbers.Primary}}</a>
        <p class="legal-numbers__label">India's national emergency number for police, fire and ambulance.</p>
      </div>
      {{if .Numbers.HasOlder}}
      <div class="legal-numbers__row">
        <p class="legal-numbers__number">{{.Numbers.OlderList}}</p>
        <p class="legal-numbers__label">{{.OlderLabel}}</p>
        <p class="legal-numbers__note">Many state governments still list these and they may still work in your state, but some states have retired them. Try {{.Numbers.Primary}} first.</p>
      </div>
      {{end}}
      {{if .Numbers.HasStateLines}}
      <div class="legal-numbers__row">
        <p class="legal-numbers__number">{{.Numbers.StateHelpline}} and {{.Numbers.DistrictHelpline}}</p>
        <p class="legal-numbers__label">For floods and cyclones, many states use {{.Numbers.StateHelpline}} for the state disaster helpline and {{.Numbers.DistrictHelpline}} for the district control room.</p>
        <p class="legal-numbers__note">These vary by state. Check your state disaster management authority's website.</p>
      </div>
      {{end}}
    </section>

    <h2>How to read what Pinalert shows</h2>
    <dl class="legal-glossary">
      {{range .Glossary}}
      {{range .Terms}}<dt>{{.}}</dt>
      {{end}}<dd>{{.Text}}</dd>
      {{end}}
    </dl>

    <h2>Reports can be wrong</h2>
    <p>A report is what someone near the place says they saw. Confirmations from people nearby make it more likely to be right. They don't make it certain. Serious reports show at once, before anyone confirms them, so check how many places have confirmed a report before you rely on it. Don't make decisions about your safety from Pinalert alone.</p>

    <h2>Reports expire</h2>
    <p>After a fixed time a report is marked Expired and leaves the Nearby list, whether or not anyone confirms it. Ended reports stay under My activity, Ended nearby, for 7 days. Most reports last {{.ExpiryHours}} hours and critical reports last {{.CriticalExpiryHours}} hours. Confirmations don't extend that time.</p>

    {{if .ContactEmail}}
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p class="legal-contact">To report abuse or ask for something to be removed, write to <a href="{{.ContactHref}}">{{.ContactEmail}}</a>.</p>
    {{end}}
{{end}}

{{define "legal_policy_body"}}
    <h2 id="policy">Policy</h2>
    <p class="legal-subtitle">Rules, privacy and terms</p>

    <h2>What you can post</h2>
    <p>Post reports about emergencies and conditions you can see near you. Hateful, harassing or sexual text isn't allowed, and neither are reports made on purpose to mislead.</p>
    <p>What the automatic check rejects is narrower than what isn't allowed. Text that is clearly hateful, harassing or sexual is rejected before it is posted, or removed afterwards when the check finishes late. Text made of random characters with no real words is always rejected before it is posted. Other text that breaks these rules can still be posted, and a moderator may remove it later.</p>
    <p>Violent or frightening words are fine when they describe a real emergency. Urgent wording, capital letters, addresses and phone numbers are fine in a genuine report.</p>

    <h2>How the automatic check works</h2>
    <p>The text of a report is sent to OpenAI's moderation service. Only the description is sent, never your account, your sign in, your network address or your location. OpenAI documents no retention and no training use for moderation requests.</p>
    <p>If the text is clearly hateful, harassing or sexual, it is rejected and nothing is stored. If such text is only caught after the report was saved, because the check finished late, the report is removed instead: it stays stored but shows to no one. If the text is borderline, it is posted and a moderator may look at it.</p>
    <p>If the check can't finish in time, a normal report waits and doesn't show to anyone until it does. A critical report is published at once and checked afterwards. A Rescue needed report posted before that category was retired keeps this rule until it fades.</p>
    <p>The check can be wrong, which is why moderators exist. No photos are accepted.</p>

    <h2>What moderators can do</h2>
    <p>Moderators can read reports, keep them or remove them. A removed report shows to no one. Its author sees "Removed after review" both when a moderator removed it and when the automatic check removed it after it was saved. A flag on a report never hides it by itself. It only asks a moderator to look. The person who flagged is never shown to the author.</p>

    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>Each account can post, vote and flag reports only so fast, to stop spam. When you reach a limit, Pinalert says how long to wait and keeps what you typed.</p>

    <h2>What Pinalert keeps</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your email address, to sign you in. It is never shown to other people.</li>
      <li>Each report, with its location, its time and your account.</li>
      <li>Your votes, kept as a rough square about 150 metres wide and not as an exact point.</li>
      <li>The result and scores of the automatic check, and which model gave them, without the report text: for borderline reports and for any report whose check finished after it was saved.</li>
      <li>Flags you send, and their reasons.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Nothing listed here is deleted on a schedule today: reports, votes, flags and sign in records stay stored, and an expired report only stops showing in the lists.</p>
    {{if .ContactEmail}}
    <p>You can ask for a report or your data to be removed by writing to the address under Complaints and removal requests.</p>
    {{end}}
    <p>The map is drawn with files from unpkg.com and map tiles from OpenFreeMap, or from OpenStreetMap on devices that can't draw the vector map. A typed place search goes through Pinalert to Photon, a search service run by komoot. Pinalert sends what you typed and the position of your pin or the middle of the map. If Photon can't answer, the search goes to OpenStreetMap's Nominatim service instead. The places in the results come from OpenStreetMap. Those services see the request the way any website does.</p>

    <h2>Cookies and storage on your device</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A session cookie, set the first time you open any Pinalert page, including this one, before you sign in. It is kept up to a year, until you log out.</li>
      <li>A cookie that remembers you chose the Low data view.</li>
      <li>Your Light or Dark choice.</li>
      <li>Reports waiting to send, saved on this device until they are sent or discarded.</li>
      <li>Your last known position on the Low data view, on this device only.</li>
      <li>A short lived position kept during a visit, so voting doesn't ask again.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>There are no advertising or tracking cookies.</p>
    <p>Browsers can delete saved data, so a report waiting to send isn't guaranteed to survive. Send it as soon as you have a signal. A private window closing, low storage, or a site left unused for about a week in Safari can all clear it.</p>

    <h2>Emergencies and the police</h2>
    <p>For anything serious, such as a crime or a threat to someone's safety, contact the police directly. In an emergency call {{.Numbers.Primary}}. Pinalert doesn't contact the police for you.</p>

    {{if .ContactEmail}}
    <h2>Complaints and removal requests</h2>
    <p class="legal-contact">To report abuse or ask for a report to be removed, write to <a href="{{.ContactHref}}">{{.ContactEmail}}</a>.</p>
    {{end}}

    <h2>Terms</h2>
    <p>Using Pinalert means you accept these rules. Pinalert may remove reports that break them, and the limits apply to every account. Pinalert is provided as it is, with no promise of accuracy or availability. It is unofficial.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated {{.PolicyLastUpdated}}</p>
{{end}}
